<!-- Hero Section -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-glow"></div>
  <h1>Semantic Data Type</h1>
  <p>
    The Semantic Data Type (SDT) specification provides an intelligent bridge between data type concepts and how they are commonly represented in files, databases, and programming environments.
    By capturing key aspects—including meaning and purpose, usage, formatting, and validation rules—it enables both humans and machines to develop a deep, actionable understanding of the underlying data.
  </p>
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <a href="{{ '/library/' | url }}" class="btn btn-primary">Browse SDT Library</a>
    <a href="{{ '/playground/' | url }}" class="btn btn-secondary">Try Validator Playground</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Core Pillars -->
<h2 style="justify-content: center; margin-top: 4rem;">Core Pillars of Semantic Types</h2>
<div class="grid pillars-grid" style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="badge badge-violet" style="align-self: flex-start; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Modeling</div>
    <h3 style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Conceptual Alignment</h3>
    <p class="card-description" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
      Semantic types are aligned to standard ontologies like SKOS, Wikidata, and LCSH. They represent discrete real-world concepts, not just raw primitive data types.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="badge badge-cyan" style="align-self: flex-start; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Bindings</div>
    <h3 style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Physical Storage Mappings</h3>
    <p class="card-description" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
      Mappings defined across multiple environments, detailing how a type is stored in databases (SQL, PostgreSQL, BigQuery), represented in programming (Python, Rust, TypeScript), or exchanged (XSD).
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="badge badge-violet" style="align-self: flex-start; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Actionability</div>
    <h3 style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Agentic Skills & Instructions</h3>
    <p class="card-description" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
      Built-in instructions and system prompt snippets designed for LLMs to interpret, parse, normalize, and reason with variables matching the semantic data type.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="badge badge-cyan" style="align-self: flex-start; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Reliability</div>
    <h3 style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Algorithmic Checksums</h3>
    <p class="card-description" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
      Multi-layered validation combining structure-matching regular expressions with complex algorithmic check validations (such as Luhn, Modulo-11, and Modulo-97).
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

